   "unmapped": [
    "Arms are l heuristics for a Metrical Task System; heuristic costs f_t(i)=c_t(s_t^i)+d(s_{t-1}^i,s_t^i) in [0,2D] where D is the metric diameter",
    "m-delayed bandit access: a query returns the heuristic's state only if the same heuristic was queried in the previous m-1 steps; cost observable only after m consecutive queries",
    "learner sees the full MTS input (cost functions) with 1-step look-ahead and may take improper steps (states not suggested by any heuristic)",
    "switching between heuristics' states incurs metric movement cost up to D",
    "learner knows the diameter D and the delay parameter m",
    "regret bounded in terms of the best heuristic's cost OPT_{<=0} (small-loss type)"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "For $m \\geq 2$, we say that an algorithm $\\ALG$ has {\\em $m$-delayed bandit access} to heuristics $H_1, \\dotsc, H_\\ell$ if (i) it can query at most one heuristic $H_i$ at each time step $t$ and (ii) the query yields the current state of $H_i$ only if $H_i$ was queried also in steps $t\\!-\\!m\\!+\\!2, \\dotsc, t$, otherwise it yields an empty result."
  },
